{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/842217-hesitation-about-playing-a-modern-neonate","id":842217,"title":"Hesitation About Playing a Modern Neonate","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-04T16:12:33-08:00","id":842217,"title":"Hesitation About Playing a Modern Neonate","content":"It can be really fun to play a neonate, recently Embraced vampire in a historical time period. You have a stretch of history unfolding for you to take part in, to witness, to grow old and terrible surviving against. I find it an incredibly good time to go from Rome, or Elizabethan England, or the rise of the Ottoman Empire, or some other period, and then see what this character is going to be like when they go from a time of chariots and sails to nights of cell phones and air planes. Playing out those early neonate nights are great fun, and they're great fun in modern settings too!<br /> <br /> But there is always something unsatisfying lingering in the background about being a vampire who started out in this relatively modern era because I don't know how history is going to unfold over the next few centuries. I have trouble grasping where we're going to go from here. So, if I start as a neonate in these modern nights there isn't really anywhere forward to go. I'm not going to see how that character changes over time, because I don't even know what is going to happen next year let alone in then next 20 or 50 years. It bothers me, this realization.<br /> <br /> Has anyone else had this problem before?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T16:38:32-08:00","id":842236,"title":"","content":"I can always see the fun in the &quot;man out of time&quot; trope. However, when I'm playing a fresh Neonate, I usually have a hard time envisioning my character transitioning that quickly to the long view. Really, there's the unrelenting horror (usually) to get through. . .a lot of things, really, that need immediate attention.<br /> <br /> 1. Stave off ennui.<br /> 2. Find a steady source of blood that doesn't get you caught<br /> 3. Get out from under any undesirables you're currently under<br /> 4. Oh shit that's hard<br /> 5. Quick do something for them<br /> 6. Also. . quick, obtain some object, skill, or connections that makes you useful.<br /> <br /> <br /> Basically, most Neonates I envision playing are nowhere NEAR the slow-paced chess match of the Eldars or even the Ancillae, because they're basically still people. And their lives are basically a shitty version of Frogger, dodging the cars and trucks of their betters' plans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T16:59:04-08:00","id":842251,"title":"","content":"Oh no doubt, I just meant that I like eventually moving past those early days and seeing how they develop decades later or more and it's really hard to do that if I start in the modern day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T17:09:44-08:00","id":842256,"title":"","content":"I feel like this is more an issue with playing vampire in modern settings than neonates specifically. Basically, modern games make it hard to do time skips. This can be troublesome no matter the age of the character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T17:17:10-08:00","id":842260,"title":"","content":"And here I thought playing neonates was the default standard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T17:17:35-08:00","id":842261,"title":"","content":"Yes. If you like playing characters throughout time, you should probably stick to characters who started in the past.<br /> <br /> Not being able to jump ahead in time and show off the immortality of vampires is a problem with modern games but there's many other aspects of vampires than that. And you aren't forced to start as a neonate in a modern game, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T17:22:28-08:00","id":842268,"title":"","content":"That's about what I was expecting, these replies. It makes me curious if anyone has gone ahead and done timeskips from a modern setting anyway. Anyone have experience with that? How did you figure out what went wrong?<br /> <br /> Did you succumb to temptation like I'm doing in my imagination right now and suddenly turn the world into Fallout?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T17:27:40-08:00","id":842274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/842217-hesitation-about-playing-a-modern-neonate?p=842268#post842268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's about what I was expecting, these replies. It makes me curious if anyone has gone ahead and done timeskips from a modern setting anyway. Anyone have experience with that? How did you figure out what went wrong?<br /> <br /> Did you succumb to temptation like I'm doing in my imagination right now and suddenly turn the world into Fallout?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never done that, but I did play in a Fallout-inspired Geist game once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T17:27:53-08:00","id":842275,"title":"","content":"I've done time skips but only a few years at a time. My players pretty much all don't like historical stuff so I can't go that way and they don't like fantasy and sci-fi mixes, otherwise I'd use the Mirrors books to make some futuristic stuff. But you jump ahead ten years or so and not much is going to be different.<br /> <br /> The Mirrors books offer a post-Apocalyptic situation, a cyberpunk setting, and a space opera one. They're pretty bare bones, mostly with some basic concepts and changes splats might have but it's better than nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T17:42:28-08:00","id":842281,"title":"","content":"So I guess the idea is, if I want to do longer timeskips I'll have to just bite the bullet and make more things up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T18:19:45-08:00","id":842313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/842217-hesitation-about-playing-a-modern-neonate?p=842281#post842281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I guess the idea is, if I want to do longer timeskips I'll have to just bite the bullet and make more things up.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only other option for a modern game would be to have a 'future' book. Which, I guess, might happen, but even then I'd still expect you to have to do a lot of the work on your own. As it is, you're able to play a lot of those past periods because there's easily accessible information about them beyond the books to help flesh it out and do a lot of the work. Outside of other game settings like Shadowrun or Trinity you aren't really going to have that for the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-04-2016, 09:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T19:13:13-08:00","id":842340,"title":"","content":"The worry about the future hasn't come up in game, just in my musings.<br /> <br /> What I will suggest is that when it comes to the future, you could do as suggested and invent a sci-fi world or you could play our world and then just tack on oddities.<br /> <br /> What I mean by the latter is that you don't come out and say 'It is 2070, here is your fallout future', you simply say it is 2070. Your vampire notices some clear differences, like people have metal parts now, or plastic surgery is everywhere, or car fly but small things aren't brought up until they are inconvenient. It is easier to imagine from the other side. We are told that Elders struggle with social media. Well, one reason for this is that they don't use it; what they use still works for them, and they didn't really notice the change. So it would be with your future. The vampire asks for contact information, and instead of getting a number or username as a reply, the person activates a gadget that plays a brief melody and smiles. Do this a few times and you may even get the apt Elder response of going with the familiar over learning the new thing. When does this happen? When it suits you as ST or when the future needs to be noticed.It can even work with customs. Instead of reading about Vikings to get a sense of the time period, you are reading about them to liberally steal a custom, giving it a post-industrial twist, and passing it off as completely mundane. My hope is that would convey to players the same unease an elder would feel without forcing the game into complete sci-fi mode.<br /> <br /> Final note: Never tested this, just some thoughts on making time skips less of a worry by making them more predictable but still the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T18:54:22-08:00","id":844856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/842217-hesitation-about-playing-a-modern-neonate?p=842281#post842281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I guess the idea is, if I want to do longer timeskips I'll have to just bite the bullet and make more things up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know the details, but I do know that DaveB's mummy game takes place all over history, including up to 2160 or something like that.<br /> <br /> So yeah, make some shit up!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T22:59:22-08:00","id":844934,"title":"","content":"Has he done a write up for it, Kirby? I remember him mentioning it last year (or the one before that) but I don't think it ever showed up on RPGnet","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T04:05:37-08:00","id":845002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/842217-hesitation-about-playing-a-modern-neonate?p=842281#post842281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I guess the idea is, if I want to do longer timeskips I'll have to just bite the bullet and make more things up.</div> </div> </div> </div> Basically. What you are asking for, in effect, is a home brew futuristic setting. You might have better luck going into the general CofD forum and asking there. <br /> <br /> I believe that there was some suggestions in the Shards from the Mirrors book, but I personally found them singularly unhelpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T10:51:10-08:00","id":845165,"title":"","content":"Why not use other characters? Start as a modern neonate, go through the struggles, gain XP, have fun, then play your Sire in the time they became established as Ancilla. Then your Sire's Sire. Back and back and so forth. Just at different periods of their Requiem so XP lines up.<br /> <br /> Or play a modern neonate but don't follow conventional time or history. Yes the city changes. Yes major international events happen. They need not line up with our history. Make them major narrative points of your game possibly or just for flavor to show off their immortality. Whats important is the permanence of the Vampire and the contrasting impermanence of everything and everyone else.<br /> <br /> It worked in the Matrix, so it can work for Vampire right? They live in a world of 1999, forever. Just make 1999 last for 50 years, then move up to 2000's etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","user":"GilboD","date":". 03-10-2016, 01:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T12:53:26-08:00","id":845218,"title":"","content":"That's a fascinating idea, working backwards for the characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T13:46:47-08:00","id":845245,"title":"","content":"I don't really find it hard to do time skips. When you first are going to do a modern game take a look at all the random news stories going. In the US. There are random cites getting water poised, Terrorist attacks, Police attacks, Riots, Super Storms, Huge Fires and so on. Now think about what way you want to push your game. Maybe more riots and protests keep happening which leads to huge police crack down on freedom which leads people to try and start a new civil war. You could make it that a whole city gets messed up because radiation leaks into the water table killing people and now they all have to move to a new city which causes sickness to spread and the CDC must get involved. Now your neonate must avoid the CDC or something. <br /> <br /> In modern games its all about how you wanna push the world. You can make history how you want or you can leave it to chance by simply making a chart of 1 - 10 and give each number a good or bad thing to see how an event plays out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T07:35:49-08:00","id":845630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/842217-hesitation-about-playing-a-modern-neonate?p=842268#post842268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's about what I was expecting, these replies. It makes me curious if anyone has gone ahead and done timeskips from a modern setting anyway. Anyone have experience with that? How did you figure out what went wrong?<br /> <br /> Did you succumb to temptation like I'm doing in my imagination right now and suddenly turn the world into Fallout?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have, most modern games I set back a decade when the games start so 2001 or 1992 then play forward, but I have jumped as far as 2050. I believe some gadgets will become cooler but nothing too much will change. Wars almost start on a global scale but get called off. Once I had an active cold world War. Once I had holograms and such, but high tech is normally in the hands of the rich so not commonly seen outside of t.v","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}